 "title": "Gene Expression and Metabolism in Trypanosoma brucei and P. manshurica",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on the gene expression and metabolism of Trypanosoma brucei and P. manshurica. The gene AAT10.2 is central to this cluster, with its mRNA levels influenced by SDM79 and its phosphorylation site located in PCF T. brucei. AAT10.2 is also associated with transporters in Leishmania and Trypanosoma cruzi. P. manshurica catabolizes arginine and alanine, and produces gas. Carvacrol inhibits P. manshurica and interferes with lipid metabolism. The cluster also includes various amino acids, including BCAA, leucine, isoleucine, and valine, which are transported by AAT10.2. The relationships between these entities highlight the complex interactions between gene expression and metabolism in these organisms.",
